  "body": "Point 2 of #1056 was still open: a project saved before #911 with an over-budget STEP mesh loaded as full fidelity, with no re-check. Points 1, 3 and 4 shipped in #1127. Points 3 and 4 are checked against their pins in the issue comment.\n\n## Decision (docs/decisions/1056-fidelity-unknown.md)\n- **Re-measuring on load is not possible.** The chord error is measured against the B-rep, and the file keeps only facets.\n- **A v58 file cannot be narrowed.** #911 did not bump the version, so the file cannot tell a pre-#911 save from a later fine one, and it does not say which meshes came from STEP and which from STL/OBJ.\n- So: **\"fidelity unknown\", refused by name**. It is not tightened, because no bound on the unknown chord exists.\n\n## What changed\n- `PROJECT_VERSION` goes to **59**. Loading an older file runs `project::fidelity_migrate`, which marks every mesh without a recorded `coarse_mm` \"fidelity unknown\": models with facets, fixtures and from-model stock copies. Each marked mesh gets one load note. A recorded chord from a #911-era file is kept.\n- The mark is the sentinel chord `model_fidelity::UNKNOWN_MM` (1e12 mm) on the existing `ReducedFidelity` component. It therefore rides every path the flag already rides: copies, setup clones, delete/undo and `UpdateModel` propagation. No path can drop it silently.\n- **Gate:** every op judged against an unknown mesh is refused by name (\"... saved before CamCraft recorded mesh fidelity (project v58 or older) ... re-import the model to verify its operations\"). An unknown part refuses the program verdict through `verdict_tol`, and an unknown fixture gets a `gate_problems` line of its own. Through `program_tol`, the program sim and the eye judge nothing.\n- **Display:** the model page, MCP `get_job` and the script API say \"Fidelity unknown\" in words (`summary`, `facts` with `fidelity_unknown: true`). The sentinel is never shown as a number.\n- **Fixtures:** an unknown fixture keeps its plain box at generation. Growing it by the sentinel would make it collide with everything, and the gate refusal blocks the post.\n- **File format:** the mark is saved as `\"fidelity_unknown\": true`, so a re-save can never turn it into \"fine\". A row carrying both `fidelity_unknown` and `coarse_mm` is corrupt and refused before any world write. Only a fresh import clears the mark, and undoing that import restores it.\n- `examples/first-part.camproj` and the microARC kit project are re-stamped v59 by hand. Their meshes are exact (an OBJ generator, and a mesh built in code), so they are known full fidelity.\n- Follow-up #1339 (P7) covers an undoable \"vouch for this mesh\" command with its MCP tool, for models whose source file is gone or whose mesh is exact.\n\n## How tested\n- Pin: `fidelity_copies::a_project_saved_before_fidelity_was_recorded_loads_unknown_and_refuses_until_reimported`. It loads a v58 file and checks:\n  - the model reads unknown (never full fidelity);\n  - the recorded chords of \"blank\" and its stock copy are kept;\n  - the load note is present;\n  - `op_problem`, the verification report, `program_tol`, `verdict_tol`, `summary` and `facts` all say the named line;\n  - a re-save writes `fidelity_unknown` (no `coarse_mm`) at v59, and that file is not migrated again;\n  - `UpdateModel` clears the mark and its undo restores it;\n  - a row with both keys is refused.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on head 65deeffd: app suites ok (175 s), ui suites ok (7 s). The run covered 94 app suites, including project_roundtrip, mcp, microarc_test_part, model_fidelity, coarse_laws, step_budget and the setup/fixture suites.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- ui lib (`--test-threads=1`): model_fidelity, step_budget, and `tool_body::the_simulated_tool_reaches_from_its_tip_into_the_body_on_the_users_document` (it loads the v56 `step_block_371.camproj`): ok.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The GUI by hand: opening a real pre-#911 project and reading the load notes and the model page line.\n- The release-lane gpu_render docs test, which opens `examples/first-part.camproj`. Only that file's version number changed.\n\n## Breaking\n- Older builds refuse a v59 file (the version check), as with every version bump.\n- Every project saved before v59 refuses its operations until each model is re-imported. That cost is deliberate; #1339 tracks removing it.\n\nChangelog: Projects saved before mesh fidelity was recorded (v58 or older) open with each model marked \"fidelity unknown\" and their operations refused by name until the model is re-imported, instead of being judged as full fidelity (project v59) (#1056)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0; branch merged with upstream/main.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: projects saved before v59 refuse their operations until each mesh is re-imported (project v59 marks un-recorded meshes \"fidelity unknown\"; follow-up #1339 adds a vouch command).\n\nFixes #1056\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n\n",
